  "label": "general internet audience",
  "description": "The meme is designed for a broad, general internet audience familiar with common domestic experiences and religious imagery. The humor relies on universal relatability — the feeling of impatience while waiting for cookies to bake — which transcends specific demographics or communities. The target audience includes anyone who has experienced the mundane frustration of waiting for food to bake, and who can appreciate the absurd contrast between a solemn Catholic Mass and that trivial waiting. The meme does not target any specific cultural, religious, racial, gender, or identity-based group; it is accessible to anyone with basic understanding of baking and church ceremonies.",
